  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context and rigor">Declare rigor FULL. Read the notes of 043, 044, 045, 046, 047, 072, 073 for their final contracts. Write a one-page step-to-component map in notes before coding; if contracts do not compose, escalate.</step>
    <step order="1">Handler: parse payload {submissionId}; flag check; idempotency re-read; call the processor; map results to JobOutcome.</step>
    <step order="2">Processor steps 1-5: set Processing; ReadInvoiceAsync; compare the read firm invoice number with the typed one (D-91); map to 046 input and resolve; code lines (047); evaluate (072) with resolved lines and combined confidence; decide (073).</step>
    <step order="3">Persist Accepted: one transaction for invoice (In Review, firm, core-record fields, tracking number, correlation id), lines (line type, timekeeper, codes, coding confidence, extraction-confidence JSON per FR-04 from 043's per-field confidence / page / bounding box), approval portion (021 columns; approvers are 103's), document invoice link; then 016 totals; then Signals via SignalWriter; then submission Accepted with sprk_invoice.</step>
    <step order="4">Persist Rejected: submission Rejected, reason code, findings JSON (finding, line, values read, rule, version, clause) for 130 / 133; no invoice.</step>
    <step order="5">After steps: enqueue InvoiceIndexing for accepted invoices (its handler is registered only when DocumentIntelligence:Enabled — FinanceModule.cs:186-189; record behaviour when absent); call IEbillingNotificationSink (no-op) for Accepted and Rejected.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests: accepted path writes everything once; rejected path writes no invoice; failure injected after line creation leaves no invoice and status Failed or retry; re-delivery after Accepted is a no-op; re-delivery after a Signal-write failure completes Signals without a second invoice; each read reason code; flag off; missing tracking number allocation; Null AI facade → Failed with ai.invoice.disabled.</step>
    <step order="7">Run the job end to end in a local or dev environment on one sample invoice if the deploy task has not yet run; otherwise leave to 053. Build, test, publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="9">Record deviations (transaction vs compensation, Signal ordering, assumptions) in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the component contracts from 043, 046, 047, 072, 073, 014 or 016 do not compose (missing field, conflicting confidence model, evaluator needs data the pipeline does not have), STOP and escalate with the step-to-component map rather than adapting a component silently.</trigger>
    <trigger>If neither ExecuteTransaction nor a reliable compensation can give all-or-nothing for invoice + lines + approval + link, STOP: FR-20's acceptance cannot be met and the owner must choose.</trigger>
    <trigger>If writing Signals inside the same all-or-nothing unit is required by the owner (rather than idempotent after-commit as specified here), STOP and escalate with ontology-r1 (SignalWriter is ontology-owned).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>InvoiceExtractionJobHandler creates invoice data from email-derived candidates via the legacy extraction path; no handler runs the eBilling pipeline. No notification seam for eBilling exists.</existing>
    <extension>The legacy handler is tied to InvoiceAnalysisService and the review-confirm flow and is retired by 050; extending it would keep the legacy contract alive. The notification sink is a one-method seam so 132 can plug in without editing the processor.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>FR-20 fails: submissions stay Received forever, no invoice is ever created from SPA or internal submission, and the R1 loop does not exist.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

